    "node_id": "I_kwDORdC75M8AAAABMFk89Q",
    "title": "ix patches is registered nowhere — registerPatchesCommand is dead code",
    "body": "Found by @Alot1z while writing the agent skill (#368).\n\n\\`ix-cli/src/cli/commands/patches.ts:6\\` exports \\`registerPatchesCommand\\`, but nothing imports it — it is absent from \\`ix-cli/src/cli/register/oss.ts\\`. So \\`ix patches\\` is an unknown command today.\n\nIt is also listed in \\`PRO_COMMANDS\\` in \\`oss.ts\\`, which means \\`registerProStubs\\` currently installs the \"requires Ix Pro\" stub for it. Users on Pro presumably get the real one; users on OSS get the Pro message rather than an unknown-command error, which is why this has gone unnoticed.\n\nDecide which it is:\n- If \\`patches\\` is meant to be OSS, register it in \\`oss.ts\\` and drop it from \\`PRO_COMMANDS\\`.\n- If it is meant to be Pro-only, delete \\`patches.ts\\` from this repo so the stub is the only implementation.\n\nNote the file already carries a complete \\`--format <fmt>\\` declaration advertising \\`llm\\`, with no llm renderer behind it — see the \\`--format llm\\` coverage issue.",
